  "structural_change": "S81-ELEM2-HWIN successor of dsdv_mu_hwin_c21r (daemon NEEDS_RTL: c21q TT -148.19 / FF -8.26, c21r TT -141.73 / FF -11.76, DRC 0). Failing class: g_compare_copy.cmp_r -> 47-entry identity compare + OR reduce -> global duplicate flag udup -> distributed to all 16x2 event rec_r + slot record_group across the 561.6 um band (two 113/148 ps buffer hops, arrival 1222.75 vs required 1081.02). Fix (RTL, codex adf49d4f8 LOCAL_RECORD=1): each of the (NEV/4 event + 6 slot) record consumer groups gets its own kept duplicate-region cone (2 local 10-bit user landing flops, 47 compares, 8-entry partial ORs), so admission drives <= 8 local record flops instead of a band-wide broadcast; 0 cycles added (waveform miter vs frozen HWIN21cb + anchor). NEV 16 fallback on the unchanged c21r 84-SRAM geometry (superset of the die's 8 events). Physical: c21j hash-locked native manifests/fences dropped (cannot qualify changed RTL); c21h row-pruned band + GPL row envelope instead; pd 0.55; OPT_POST_GRT_WNS=0 pre_grt kept (EST-0104 class). Clock structural successor to c22r complete raw endpoint-envelope failure TT106.0/FF111.5 ps and macro slew349.9/360.8 ps. Each actual SRAM clock pin receives a dedicated physical driven leaf. Symmetric physical buffer branches distribute the same source clock to SRAMs and bounded local flop leaves. No clock-target or limit change; exact complete TT/FF envelope and macro slew must be measured.",
  "pin_regs": {
    "enable": false,
    "reason": "Source-registered: f_ks / f_mc / f_mw / mu_rt land in pin flops (ks_q / mc_q / mw_q / rt_q), mu_c / mu_rc / t_wf leave flops (c_q / rc_q / t_wf)."
  },
